SUMMARY:Fellows Singers
DESCRIPTION:The Fellows Singers is a local chamber choir founded in 2017. F
 rom September\, Jonathan Darbourne\, Artistic Director of Vache Baroque\, 
 becomes its Director of Music. The range of music covered is broad from ea
 rly English madrigals to classic pop via old English folk songs and operat
 ic choruses. Concerts take place three times a year and in addition there 
 are opportunities for solos for those who wish to sing them. The choir als
 o leads the carol service at St Saviours Chruch\, Eton Road.\n\nThey are a
  friendly community of amateur singers at various levels of experience\, a
 lthough some experience of singing in choirs is desirable. The Fellows Sin
 gers are looking for new members\, especially male voices.\n\nRehearsals t
 ake place on Tuesday evenings\, mostly in the Primrose Hill Community Libr
 ary\, starting on 24 September. Approximate costs per term (10 sessions pl
 us concert) are £120 including room hire and fee to the music director (d
 epending on numbers in the choir). An additional fee for an accompanist at
  the concert\, which takes place at St Saviours Church\, would be about £
 10 per person. Please contact Jeremy Lewison on 07901 555 785\, jeremy@jer
 emylewison.co.uk for further information.
CATEGORIES:Events for adults
LOCATION:Primrose Hill Community Library\, Primrose Hill Community Library\
 , 11-16 Sharples Hall St\, Primrose Hill\, London\, Greater London\, NW1 8
 YN\, United Kingdom
